(project tuna-federation
 (doc "Tuna book chapter: federation - two tuna instances speak trees. Pre-registered as a sketch so the substrate never grows a feature that forecloses it. Thesis: the ops chain (genesis-anchored, hash-linked, prefix-folded, tamper-verified) is the replicable unit; peers exchange values by hash and converge by shipping verified ops windows, not by inventing a second protocol.")
 (* agent note (|2026-09-18, M12 opens with F1 implemented: GET
    /api/fed/value/:hash answers {hash, kind, payload} for tree
    (canonical ternary; a program hash resolves as its own ternary -
    one address law) and bytes (base64).  Reads stay hash-gated
    (byte-values law 2), so any valid bearer identity may fetch and
    there is no new authz model; per-peer identities come from
    TUNA_FED_PEERS at boot (absent names get a generated token printed
    once, the root bootstrap pattern; names are lowercase alnum +
    dashes and gate ns/<peer>/ prefixes later).  Every answer, 404s
    included, lands in the ops chain as op "fed-value" attributed to
    the calling identity, so a peer's fetches are visible in the
    audited log.  Client side: scripts/fed-pull.sh rehashes the
    payload (openssl sha256) and fails loudly on mismatch or 404 -
    rejects are never absorbed.  Acceptance: tests/fed_tests.ml (6
    green, own scratch db) + dev-instance e2e (bytes fetch by a peer
    token, ops row carries the peer actor).|) *)
 (status in-progress)
 (convention ocaml-dune)
 (section federation
  (doc "Three phases, each independently shippable, each with pre-registered failure. F1 implemented 2026-09-18; F2 and F3 still out of scope.")
  (status in-progress)
  (subsection phases
   (status in-progress)
   (details
    (doc (|
      F1 VALUE EXCHANGE (read-only, IMPLEMENTED 2026-09-18). GET
         /api/fed/value/:hash returns {hash, kind, payload} for either
         kind (tree ternary, bytes base64; a program hash resolves as
         its own ternary); the peer rehashes on receipt and trusts
         nothing but the hash (scripts/fed-pull.sh). Per-peer bearer
         identities via TUNA_FED_PEERS; hash-gated reads (byte-values
         law 2) mean no new authz model; fetches journal as op
         "fed-value" attributed to the calling identity.
      F2 OPS-CHAIN SYNC. Pull: GET /api/fed/ops?prefix=&after_seq=
         returns op windows with op_hash linkage a peer can verify
         (mid-log windows verify internal-linkage-only, genesis anchor
         for seq 1 - the d7e0ae7 lesson, pinned). Push: POST
         /api/fed/ops/apply accepts a verified window into a
         peer-scoped namespace ns/<peer>/... and re-derives the index
         by fold. Per-peer authz = one prefix grant per peer. Conflict
         law v0: append-only per namespace, no merge - divergence is
         visible as two namespaces, never silently reconciled.
      F3 PRICKLYPEAR BRIDGE. Align attribution first (PP acted_by,
         still unshipped), then bearer parity (PP delegated Bearer ==
         tuna identity token), then a PP prims library calling
         /api/tree/* and /api/fed/* so PP rows and tuna paths cite each
         other by id/hash without either store encoding the other's
         internals. PP is a client of the tree surface before it is a
         peer of the chain. |))))
  (subsection pre-registered-failures
   (status planned)
   (details
    (doc (|
      1. Two peers diverge on the same path and no check notices ->
         failure; divergence must surface as distinct namespaces or a
         verified rejection.
      2. An applied op that fails rehash or chain-linkage verification
         -> failure; rejects are journaled, never absorbed.
      3. A bridge write attributed to any identity other than the true
         actor (or its delegated identity) -> failure. |))))))
